{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"sultanlike-doughty-civet","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe `commit-msg` hook install command documented in AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md is WORKTREE-UNSAFE.\nIt silently clobbers the shared, pre-commit-managed hook for EVERY worktree, and the damage is\ninvisible until a Gerrit push is rejected for a missing `Change-Id`.\n\nThe documented command:\n\n    curl -sLo \"$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/commit-msg)\" https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/tools/hooks/commit-msg && chmod +x \"$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/commit-msg)\"\n\n`git rev-parse --git-path hooks/commit-msg` run from inside a linked worktree does NOT resolve to that\nworktree — hooks live in the shared common dir, so it resolves to `/…/rebar/.git/hooks/commit-msg`.\nThe curl therefore OVERWRITES the pre-commit wrapper in the main checkout.\n\n## Why the damage is worse than one broken worktree\n\n`.pre-commit-config.yaml:16-19` documents the intended arrangement explicitly: pre-commit installs in\nMIGRATION mode, preserving Gerrit's hook as `commit-msg.legacy` and running BOTH, and warns \"never\ninstall with `-f`/`--overwrite`, which would drop the Change-Id stamp and break every push to Gerrit.\"\nThe curl achieves exactly that forbidden state by a different route — it replaces the wrapper rather\nthan chaining to it, so the pre-commit `commit-msg` gate (the 50/72 message rule) stops running, and\nonce someone later reinstalls pre-commit over it the Gerrit stamper is the half that disappears.\n\nEither way the failure is SILENT at commit time and only surfaces at `git push gerrit`, potentially\nmany commits later, in a DIFFERENT worktree than the one that ran the curl.\n\n## Evidence: this is not hypothetical, it happened twice in one session\n\nTwo independent agents, working different tickets in different worktrees, each ran the documented\ncommand and each clobbered `/Users/joeoakhart/rebar/.git/hooks/commit-msg`. Both noticed and repaired\nit with `make hooks`, and the repaired state was verified both times:\n\n    commit-msg          641 bytes   pre-commit wrapper\n    commit-msg.legacy  3127 bytes   Gerrit stamper, contains the Change-Id logic\n\nThey noticed because they were told to report side effects. An agent not told to look would have left\nthe repo with Change-Id stamping broken for every worktree on the host.\n\n## Approach\n\nMake the documented command worktree-correct and non-destructive. Options to weigh, not yet decided:\n\n- Resolve the shared hooks dir deliberately and refuse to overwrite a pre-commit wrapper, instructing\n  the user to run `make hooks` instead.\n- Fold the Gerrit hook install into `make hooks` so there is ONE documented way to get both hooks and\n  it is idempotent — this is the likely right answer, since `make hooks` already owns the chained\n  arrangement.\n- Have the command write `commit-msg.legacy` directly when a pre-commit wrapper is present.\n\nWhichever is chosen, the docs in AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md must stop telling contributors to curl\nover `--git-path hooks/commit-msg`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Running the documented install from inside a linked worktree leaves BOTH hooks functional: the\n      pre-commit wrapper and the Gerrit Change-Id stamper.\n- [ ] A test or scripted check asserts that after the documented install, a commit made in a worktree\n      receives a `Change-Id` AND is subject to the pre-commit `commit-msg` gate.\n- [ ] AGENTS.md and CONTRIBUTING.md no longer instruct a bare curl over\n      `$(git rev-parse --git-path hooks/commit-msg)`.\n- [ ] The failure mode is made loud rather than silent: attempting the unsafe overwrite warns or\n      refuses instead of succeeding quietly.\n- [ ] make lint and make typecheck pass by exit code; the default selection is green.","id":"84aa-bc0d-a719-4724","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"The documented commit-msg hook install is worktree-unsafe and silently clobbers Change-Id stamping for every worktree"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785709876367139001,"uuid":"36036ebd-6429-471a-a783-ba9bb50b3491"}